{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R4"],
      "pins": ["R4.1", "R4.2"],
      "nets": ["REG_SW", "REG_FB"],
      "obs": "On the Power sheet, R4 = 19k6 is drawn as a resistor bridging the buck switch node (REG_SW, left of L1) and the regulator feedback node (REG_FB, between R5 and R6). The intended divider is R5 (6k8, output→FB) and R6 (1k3, FB→GND), as stated by the sheet note 'Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6)'. A 19k6 resistor from the switch node (whose DC average equals Vout) to FB appears in parallel with R5, giving R5||R4 ≈ 5.05 kΩ and Vout = 0.8*(1+5.05/1.3) ≈ 3.9 V, not the 5 V the design calls for. The feedback position should hold only R5/R6 (a feedforward capacitor, if any), not a 19k6 resistor.",
      "expected": "The 5 V rail should be set by R5/R6 alone (Vout = 0.8*(1+R5/R6) ≈ 5 V), with no DC resistor from the switch/output node to FB; the MIC26903 app note quoted on the sheet uses only R5 and R6.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Power sheet: 'R4 19k6' resistor between REG_SW and REG_FB; note 'Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6)' with R5 6k8, R6 1k3"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "§4 item 3: 'feedback divider relation \"Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6)\"'; '5 V rail ... 9A @ 5V max.'"}
      ],
      "impact": "The 5 V servo/power rail would regulate to roughly 3.9 V instead of 5 V, under-powering the PCA9685 servo bank and the 5 V distribution, and leaving only ~0.6 V headroom for the 3V3 LDO; a clear deviation from the intended 5 V rail.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the schematic matches the spec (dual-MCU parts, sensor addresses, XT60/INA219 shunt, crystal, boot/reset switches, and the documented baro RESET/EOC swap), but the buck feedback network contains an extra 19k6 resistor R4 from the switch node to FB that parallels R5 and forces the 5 V rail to about 3.9 V, contradicting the sheet's own 'Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6)' note and the spec's 5 V rail."
}

